# evm-bench 219, regular block layout, committed-matrix discharge, Fast profile, 2026-09-17, M4 Max; contracts with the transcript copying calldata in pieces and the consistency scratch left unfilled.
# First the single-call contracts (FlockLift, FlockMatrix) in revm 43.0.2 under Osaka rules with the gas cap, block limit and code-size limit lifted, as a reference;
# then the staged verifier (verifier/src/staged) in a second EVM under Osaka rules with the transaction gas cap (EIP-7825, 2^24) and the code-size limit (EIP-170) in force.
# Each staged transaction's item range was the largest that fits the cap, found by simulating it; every gas figure below is a committed transaction's, calldata included (21,000 plus 4 per zero byte, 16 per nonzero).
# The staged lift's recorded claim hash was checked equal to the single-call lift contract's output, and the matrix session ended with the lift accepted.
# The lift was read from a cache proved earlier the same day by this binary. Gas is deterministic; the wall-clock lines are not measurements.

